---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ModelComparison from '../../components/ModelComparison.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Model Comparison Tool"
  description="Compare Claude, GPT-4o, Gemini, and Llama side by side on price and context window — sortable, no signup."
>
  <ModelComparison client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Choosing the right model</h2>
  <p>
    Picking an AI model isn't just about capability — cost and context
    window size often matter just as much for production use. A cheaper
    model with a smaller context window might be the better fit for short,
    high-volume tasks, while a larger context window matters for
    document-heavy or long-conversation use cases.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this table</h2>
  <p>
    Click a sort button to reorder models by input price, output price, or
    context window size. This makes it easy to spot the cheapest option for
    your workload, or the model with enough room for your longest documents.
  </p>

  <h2>AI Model Comparison FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Why do input and output prices differ?</strong> Generating
    output (the model "thinking" and writing) is more compute-intensive than
    reading input, so output tokens are typically priced 3-5x higher.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Is a bigger context window always better?</strong> Not
    necessarily — larger context windows can mean slower responses and, on
    some providers, higher effective cost if you're not using the full
    window efficiently.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
